talking backstage.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.901
You've been around the world
in like the last couple weeks.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.868
Do you have any idea
where you are right now?

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.434
-I'm in sunny New York.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.100
-Yeah, sunny -- [ Laughs ]
-What a beautiful day.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.534
-Sunny New York, yeah.
-I know.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:19.501
-How was the travels?

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.801
-It's been a challenge.

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.434
It's been so much fun.
I'm doing this show.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.234
We're traveling.
I've been to Africa,

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:27.167
North America, Asia,
and Australia.

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.300
And Australia, you know...
-Gorgeous.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.868
-...beautiful place.
The only thing,

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.767
of course, is that

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.267
everything will kill you
or hurt you.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.000
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no, I'm a little afraid of,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.434
yeah, because, yeah, if you swim
in the ocean, sharks.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.968
-I was swimming
in the Great Barrier Reef

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.100
and, of course, then you look
down, there is a shark,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.801
which, they keep telling you,
it's fine.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.834
[ Laughter ]
And then you read the news
and someone was --

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:49.968
No, it's not fine.
-No, that's not fine.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.100
What are you talking about?
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.467
You have something
that happened to you.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:55.667
-Oh, yeah, no, because I was
being so cautious

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.167
with everything,

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.601
but I got bitten
by these mosquitoes.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.634
And mosquitoes like, you know,
it's fine.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:01.434
-Of course.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:02.767
-And, you know, it reacted.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.868
It got kind of big, but I was
like, "Okay, it's fine."

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.767
We kept traveling.
We went to Vietnam.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.567
It got worse, and then these
blisters started forming

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.200
[ Ewws ]
and it got even -- Yeah,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.601
[ Laughter ]
it's disgusting.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.234
And then I was going to Japan

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:18.968
and, on the flight there,
it started oozing like --

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.334
[ Ewws ]
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter ]
But really, like, literally,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.067
it's like I was peeing my knees
or something.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.634
[ Ewws ]
I don't know how to explain it.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.267
-You just did.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.400
We get it. We get it.
We get it, yeah.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.734
-Anyway, I make it to Japan
and a place called Takeshima

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.434
and I say, "I think
I should see a doctor."

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.033
-Something's wrong, yeah.
-So we found,

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.601
went to this place, this doctor.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.434
I mean,
even in the waiting room,

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:44.701
there's a kid walked past,

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.133
looked at my knees like, "Oh!"

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.033
[ Laughter ]
With tears in his eyes.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.100
So, I come in,
but then this doctor,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.000
